title: "Factory-to-Customer Shipping Route Efficiency Analysis for Nassau Candy Distributor"
abstract: >-
  A data-driven analysis of factory-to-customer shipping routes for Nassau Candy
  Distributor, transforming 10,194 raw order and shipment records into route-level
  operational intelligence. The project computes seven route-level Key Performance
  Indicators (KPIs) including Average Lead Time, Delay Frequency, and Route
  Efficiency Score; performs geographic bottleneck detection across U.S. states;
  compares ship mode performance; and delivers an interactive Streamlit dashboard,
  a research paper, and an executive summary. The analytical pipeline is
  reproducible and includes data cleaning, feature engineering, route aggregation,
  efficiency benchmarking, and visualization modules.
