  abstract: >-
    This work presents a route-level efficiency analysis of factory-to-customer
    shipping operations for Nassau Candy Distributor. Using 10,194 shipment
    records spanning five factories and over fifty U.S. states, the study
    defines seven Key Performance Indicators, applies geographic bottleneck
    detection, and evaluates ship mode performance trade-offs. The pipeline
    is delivered as an interactive Streamlit dashboard alongside a reproducible
    data processing codebase, providing a data-driven foundation for logistics
    decision-making.
